
# P4: GitHub README and Version Tags

## Aim
To connect a local Git repository to GitHub and create a version tag.

## Commands and Implementation

### 1. Add GitHub Remote Repository
```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/MyPortfolio.git
```

### 2. Push Main Branch to GitHub
```bash
git push -u origin main
```

### 3. Create Version Tag
```bash
git tag -a v1.0 -m "First portfolio release"
```

### 4. Push Tag to GitHub
```bash
git push origin v1.0
```

### 5. View Available Tags
```bash
git tag
```

### 6. View Remote Repository
```bash
git remote -v
```

Replace USERNAME with your GitHub username.

